    "text": "A block of mass <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is kept at the origin at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and is having velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in the positive <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> -direction. The only force on it is a conservative and its potential energy is defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></math>. Its velocity when the force acting on it is minimum (after the time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> ) is -",
    "image": null
